  ⛔ THE ATTACH ROUTE, BECAUSE THE ASK ROUTE IS REFUSED.

  UsbManager.requestPermission on a Pixel 11 Pro Fold running Android 17 answers
  NOT GRANTED IN TWENTY MILLISECONDS AND SHOWS NO DIALOG — confirmed by watching
  the screen while it ran, not only in a log. It answers the same way from a
  service and from a visible, focused, foreground Activity; there is no
  remembered refusal (user_permissions is empty), the screen is unlocked and
  usb_data_status is enabled.

  So permission is taken the other way round. A device named here, attached while
  this application is installed, makes the system offer this application to the
  user. Accepting grants the permission PERSISTENTLY, and requestPermission is
  never involved.

  ⚠ IT COSTS A REPLUG. The offer is made when the device is attached, so a
  headset already plugged in when the APK was installed will not produce one
  until it is unplugged and plugged back.
-->
<resources>
    <!--
      The camera a VITURE Beast carries: a Sonix part, 0c45:6368, measured by
      cmd/xrcam. It is NOT a VITURE device — the headset arrives as three, and
      the camera is its own chip with its own vendor.

      ⚠ ANOTHER HEADSET NEEDS ITS OWN LINE. This matches one camera by its ids
      rather than matching every UVC device by class, and deliberately: the
      device class of a composite camera is 0xef/0x02/0x01, which is shared by a
      great many things that are not cameras, and a filter that broad would have
      this application offered every time anybody plugs in a webcam, a headset or
      a docking station.
    -->
    <usb-device vendor-id="3141" product-id="25448" />
</resources>
